# Allowed govulncheck findings in the child binaries hack/release/stage.sh stages.
#
# stage.sh scans every staged Go child (govulncheck -mode=binary) after staging
# and before signing, and reds on any finding whose trace reaches a vulnerable
# symbol in the binary unless a line below names it. One entry per line:
#
#   <GO-id> <child> <child-version> <reason> <expiry YYYY-MM-DD>
#
# <child> is the staged name (helm without its version suffix) and
# <child-version> the pin it was built or downloaded at, so a pin bump makes the
# entry match nothing and the finding is reviewed again. The reason is required
# (at least 20 characters) and says why shipping the finding is acceptable until
# the expiry, which is at most 120 days out. An expired entry is a red. An entry
# that matches no symbol-level finding in a scan is a red too: delete it, so
# exemptions do not outlive what they excused.
#
# zot v2.1.22 links golang.org/x/net v0.59.0, whose HTTP/2 code carries the five
# GO-2026-66xx findings (fixed in v0.60.0), and go.opentelemetry.io/otel v1.46.0
# (GO-2026-6505, no fixed version upstream). All six were reviewed in the
# k3sm#815 security review; the x/net fix is a zot build against v0.60.0.
GO-2026-6603 zot v2.1.22 golang.org/x/net v0.59.0 HTTP/2 Trailer memory exhaustion, exposed only on the loopback registry address where zot serves HTTP/2; fixed in v0.60.0, rebuild of zot against it pending (k3sm#815 security review) 2026-11-15
GO-2026-6610 zot v2.1.22 golang.org/x/net v0.59.0 HTTP/2 transport framing headers, exposed only on the loopback registry address where zot serves HTTP/2; fixed in v0.60.0, rebuild of zot against it pending (k3sm#815 security review) 2026-11-15
GO-2026-6611 zot v2.1.22 golang.org/x/net v0.59.0 HTTP/2 repeated window changes, exposed only on the loopback registry address where zot serves HTTP/2; fixed in v0.60.0, rebuild of zot against it pending (k3sm#815 security review) 2026-11-15
GO-2026-6612 zot v2.1.22 golang.org/x/net v0.59.0 HTTP/2 double flow control refund, exposed only on the loopback registry address where zot serves HTTP/2; fixed in v0.60.0, rebuild of zot against it pending (k3sm#815 security review) 2026-11-15
GO-2026-6617 zot v2.1.22 golang.org/x/net v0.59.0 HTTP/2 HPACK encoder race, exposed only on the loopback registry address where zot serves HTTP/2; fixed in v0.60.0, rebuild of zot against it pending (k3sm#815 security review) 2026-11-15
GO-2026-6505 zot v2.1.22 go.opentelemetry.io/otel v1.46.0 otlptrace exporter endpoint URL logging, which concerns an OTLP endpoint URL k3sm never configures for zot; no fixed version upstream, accepted until one ships (k3sm#815 security review) 2026-11-15
